{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees, to give you this land to inherit it</b>. I have already explained this (Ramban on Genesis 11:28): that He says, from the time I brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees and performed a miracle for you, the will was before Me to give you this land. And now He did not decree that He would give it to him, but said that He brought him out of Ur of the Chaldees on the condition that He would give it to him. Therefore Abraham feared lest there be a stipulation of deeds in the inheritance of the land — even though He had said to him twice (above 12:7, 13:15), \"To your seed I will give this land\" — for now He does not decree the gift as He decreed the seed to him. Therefore he said, \"By what shall I know that I shall inherit it?\" — and this is not like the question \"What is the sign?\" (II Kings 20:8). And also the Holy One, blessed be He, did not do with him as with the rest of the signs, to show him a sign or a wonder in a miraculous thing; rather, Abraham asked to know with true knowledge that he would inherit it, and that neither his sin nor the sin of his seed would cause it to be withheld from them, or perhaps the Canaanites would repent and He would fulfill in them \"At one moment I may speak concerning a nation and concerning a kingdom, to pluck up and to break down, to destroy and to overthrow, but if that nation turns from its evil, I relent of the evil\" (Jeremiah 18:7–8). And the Holy One, blessed be He, cut a covenant with him that he would inherit it in any case."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The word תנאי (stipulation/condition) appears twice in this comment; rendered consistently as 'stipulation' to preserve the technical force."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:39.893306209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}